From: Stage C <stage-c@example.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 22:46:26 +1030
Subject: [PATCH] Lower wasm memory.grow and memory.size calls

Cranelift has no opcode for wasm's memory.grow or memory.size, so a frontend cannot express them as instructions. Recognize direct calls to two reserved test-case names and replace them with the instructions instead of a call.

The reserved names carry no signature ambiguity beyond the call's signature, which is checked against the instruction's operand types. Calls must not be tail calls, which cannot return the instruction's result.

This lets cg_clif lower core::arch::wasm32::{memory_grow,memory_size} without a Cranelift change; the accompanying cg_clif patch calls these names.
